# Copy to .env; docker compose reads it automatically. Never commit .env.
#
# The NATS password of the WedaNode you are connecting to, for local development with
# docker-compose.yml. The repository keeps it empty, so this file supplies it.
#
# An image built for delivery has the password written in at build time and needs none of this.
#
# It is a property of the device, not of this example: the password of the local WedaNode is
# dmagent's NATS_PASSWORD. On the device, print it with
#   grep NATS_PASSWORD /opt/Advantech/dmagent/docker-compose.yml
# and copy the value after the '='. It differs per device, so read it on each one. UserPassword
# is the default; a node may instead use a token, a credentials file or a TLS certificate, in
# which case ask whoever runs it for the matching settings.
#
# Leaving it empty is not blocked: compose still runs, and the container reports the
# authentication failure in its own log. Nothing else in compose depends on this value, so
# `down`, `ps` and `logs` work whether or not it is filled in.
WEDA_NATS_PASSWORD=

# The SubNode name. Names are unique per organisation, so the deployment compose defaults to
# <baked name>-${EDGESYNC_EDGE_ID}, the device id the edge agent injects when it deploys a stack.
# Nothing injects it over SSH, so set a name here for a by-hand run.
SUBNODE_NAME=
